The paper investigates a coupled non-degenerate Kirchhoff system defined by the equations:
\begin{equation}\label{P} \left \{ \begin{aligned}
&\displaystyle y_{tt}-\upvarphi\Big(\int_\Omega | \nabla y |^2\,dx\Big)\Delta y
+\upalpha \Delta \uptheta=0, &\mbox{ in }&\; \Omega \times (0, +\infty)\\
&\displaystyle \uptheta_t-\Delta \uptheta-\upbeta \Delta y_t =0, &\mbox{ in
}&\; \Omega \times (0, +\infty)\\ &\displaystyle y=\uptheta=0,\; &\mbox{ on
}&\;\partial\Omega\times(0, +\infty)\\ %&\displaystyle y=0,\; &\mbox{ on
}&\;\partial\Omega\times(0, +\infty)\\ %&\displaystyle \partial_\nu y=0,
&\mbox{ on }&\;\Gamma_1\times(0, +\infty)\\ &\displaystyle y(\cdot, 0)=y_0, \;
y_t(\cdot, 0)=y_1,\;\uptheta(\cdot, 0)=\uptheta_0, \; \; &\mbox{ in }&\;
\Omega\\ \end{aligned} \right. \end{equation}
where $\Omega$ represents a bounded open subset of $\mathbb{R}^n$, $\upalpha$ and $\upbeta$ are nonzero real numbers sharing the same sign, and the function $\upvarphi$ is defined as $\upvarphi(s)= \mathfrak{m}_0+\mathfrak{m}_1s$ with positive constants $\mathfrak{m}_0$ and $\mathfrak{m}_1$. We demonstrate the existence of solutions and prove their exponential decay. This approach relies on the multiplier technique alongside specific integral inequalities attributed to Haraux and Komornik\cite{H1,KOM}.

This paper explores the existence of weak solutions for a Kirchhoff-type problem governed by a nonlocal elliptic operator within a fractional Orlicz-Sobolev space, subject to homogeneous Dirichlet boundary conditions. The problem is formulated as:
{\small$$
(D_{K,A}) \hspace*{0.5cm} \left\{
\begin{array}{clclc}
M\left( \displaystyle \int_{\R^{2N}}A\left( [u(x)-u(y)] K(x,y)\right)
dxdy\right) \mathcal{L}^K_A u & = & f(x,u) & \text{ in }& \Omega,
\hspace*{7cm} u & = & 0 \hspace*{0.2cm} \hspace*{0.2cm} & \text{ in } &
\R^N\setminus \Omega.
\label{eq1}
\end{array}
\right. $$ }
In this context, $\mathcal{L}^K_A$ denotes a nonlocal operator featuring a singular kernel $K$, while $A$ represents an $N$-function, and $\Omega$ is defined as an open, bounded subset of $\R^N$ possessing a Lipschitz boundary $\partial \Omega$.

