This study investigates the asymptotic behavior of the probability $$\mathbb{P} \{
\int\limits_0^\infty \mathbb{I}\Big(B_H(s)-c_1s>q_1u,
B_H(s)-c_2s>q_2u\Big)ds>T_u\},\quad u \to \infty,$$ where $B_H$ represents a fractional Brownian motion, $c_1,c_2,q_1,q_2$ are positive constants, $H \in (0,1)$, $T_u \ge 0$ denotes a measurable function, and $\mathbb{I}(\cdot)$ signifies the indicator function.
